From: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
Subject: [PATCH] sparc64: implement DMA mmap and get_sgtable for IOMMU ops

The sun4u and sun4v dma_map_ops lack .mmap, so dma_can_mmap() returns
false and ALSA strips all MMAP access modes from PCI sound devices, e.g.
the ALi M5455 (snd-intel8x0) in the Sun Blade 1500/2500. Without MMAP
access the default dmix device and the plug conversion plugins fail.

Coherent allocations are page_address() backed lowmem pages, so the
generic dma_common_mmap and dma_common_get_sgtable helpers apply, as
on alpha and powerpc.

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
---
diff -urp a/arch/sparc/kernel/iommu.c b/arch/sparc/kernel/iommu.c
--- a/arch/sparc/kernel/iommu.c
+++ b/arch/sparc/kernel/iommu.c
@@ -763,6 +764,8 @@ static int dma_4u_supported(struct devic
 static const struct dma_map_ops sun4u_dma_ops = {
 	.alloc			= dma_4u_alloc_coherent,
 	.free			= dma_4u_free_coherent,
+	.mmap			= dma_common_mmap,
+	.get_sgtable		= dma_common_get_sgtable,
 	.map_phys		= dma_4u_map_phys,
 	.unmap_phys		= dma_4u_unmap_phys,
 	.map_sg			= dma_4u_map_sg,
diff -urp a/arch/sparc/kernel/pci_sun4v.c b/arch/sparc/kernel/pci_sun4v.c
--- a/arch/sparc/kernel/pci_sun4v.c
+++ b/arch/sparc/kernel/pci_sun4v.c
@@ -695,6 +696,8 @@ static int dma_4v_supported(struct devic
 static const struct dma_map_ops sun4v_dma_ops = {
 	.alloc				= dma_4v_alloc_coherent,
 	.free				= dma_4v_free_coherent,
+	.mmap				= dma_common_mmap,
+	.get_sgtable			= dma_common_get_sgtable,
 	.map_phys			= dma_4v_map_phys,
 	.unmap_phys			= dma_4v_unmap_phys,
 	.map_sg				= dma_4v_map_sg,
